\begin{abstract}
Primary decomposition is a very important tool of commutative algebra and geometry. In this paper we generalized some of the existing algorithms of primary decomposition developed by Eisenbud et al. (cf. [EHV]) for free modules and also filled some gaps by providing proofs of important Theorems (\ref{thmprimary}, \ref{thmprimmon}, \ref{thmprimcomp}) appeared in [EHV]. All these algorithms are programmed and implemented in {\sc Singular}.
\end{abstract}
